id: pm-beads-3cun
title: Pin the pm toolchain to 2026.9 and stop requiring a clock-stamped changelog control
description: "pm-changelog 2026.9.2 stopped stamping the wall clock. An unflagged run now emits a bare version heading, so the changelog-date verifier that demanded a clock-derived control fails against a generator that fixed the clock dependence. Pin @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.5, pm-changelog 2026.9.2, and pm-ops ^2026.9.5, and make the control assert only that the unflagged heading differs from the flagged one. Also recover two durable merge receipts that 2026.9.5 health requires because history still names them."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-05T18:02:37.513Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-05T18:03:18.724Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-05T18:03:18.708Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-05T18:03:18.708Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
resolution: "Pinned the current pm toolchain and made the changelog-date control version-tolerant, then recovered the two durable merge receipts 2026.9.5 health requires."
expected_result: "release:check and pm health --strict-exit pass against @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.5, pm-changelog 2026.9.2, and pm-ops 2026.9.5."
actual_result: "release:check is green. The date-gate suite fails 4/22 against the old clock-stamped control and passes 22/22 after the differ-from-flagged property. Fresh-clone pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers exits 0."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-05T18:03:10.197Z",pi-agent,"pm-changelog 2026.9.2 no longer stamps the wall clock. Against the old verifier the unflagged control produced '## 2026.1.2-2' and the gate demanded '## 2026.1.2-2 - 2026-09-05'.\n\nThe control now asserts only that the unflagged heading differs from the flagged one. Revert-proof on test/verify-release-changelog-date.test.ts: 18 pass / 4 fail against the old clock-stamped control; 22 pass / 0 fail after the property change.\n\n2026.9.5 health also requires durable receipts for two history references that only existed clone-locally (4c0368f9 on pm-beads-1uz3 line 14, 8c598717 on pm-beads-y76h line 7). Recovered them as hash-only tracked receipts. Fresh clone: pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers exits 0."
